    <!-- Wireless ADB: built-in pairing with Android's own wireless debugging. -->
    <string name="wireless_adb_section_title">Wireless ADB</string>
    <string name="wireless_adb_subtitle">Pair with Android\'s own wireless debugging and run shell commands as UID 2000, without the Shizuku app.</string>
    <string name="wireless_adb_explain">Wireless ADB is optional and does not replace Shizuku. It uses the same pairing flow Shizuku uses on a non-rooted phone. Android shows a six-digit code, this app proves it knows the code over a local TLS connection, and the device then trusts the app\'s key. Commands run as the ADB shell user, not as root, so UID 0 features and app-private files stay out of reach.</string>
    <string name="wireless_adb_explain_steps">Steps: 1) Enable Developer options. 2) Open Wireless debugging and turn it on. 3) Tap Pair device with pairing code. 4) Tap Pair below and type the code in the notification. Keep the Android pairing dialog open until the notification says paired.</string>
    <string name="wireless_adb_explain_notification">The code is entered in a notification on purpose. Android keeps its pairing dialog on top of the app, so on a phone the notification shade is the only place where both stay usable. The code is used once and never saved.</string>
    <string name="wireless_adb_explain_requirements">Requires Android 11 or newer, Wi-Fi enabled and notification permission. Wireless debugging turns off after a reboot: the pairing survives, but you must turn the toggle on again before reconnecting. Android 16 may also ask for local network access.</string>
    <string name="wireless_adb_explain_security">The ADB shell can read shared storage, change settings, grant permissions, install apps and inspect system services. Only connect on a device you control. Forgetting the pairing removes this app\'s stored key; you can also unpair it in the system Wireless debugging screen.</string>
    <string name="wireless_adb_explain_miui">Some Xiaomi and MIUI builds block notification replies unless notifications use the Android style. If the reply action does not appear, open the app\'s notification settings and switch the style.</string>
    <string name="wireless_adb_privileged_note">When connected, the privileged shell tier uses this connection automatically for terminal commands, Linux environment setup, package work and background jobs. The Shizuku transport stays available and is used when it is connected.</string>
